# OpenCode bridge

OpenCode runs as a local server on this VM (loopback only, port {{ opencode_port }}).
Run tasks against it with its CLI pointed at the server:

```sh
cd /workspace/<repo>   # repos live in the shared workspace folder
opencode run --server http://127.0.0.1:{{ opencode_port }} "<task>"
```

Notes for the agent:
- The command blocks until OpenCode finishes; its stdout is the result — relay it.
- Pin a model when asked: add `-m <provider/model>`. Available providers are in this
  VM's ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json (anthropic, and omlx when configured).
- OpenCode's own skills live in ~/.agents/skills; keep them out of Hermes' view.
- Keep tasks scoped: one repo, one clear instruction. Multi-step work is fine —
  OpenCode plans and executes inside its own session, bounded by the permissions in
  this VM's opencode.json.
